{"id": "86322", "name": "תחום הגדרה – שורש של טרינום ריבועי במכנה (ב) (באנגלית)", "defaultgrade": 1, "penalty": 0, "options": {"multiplicationsign": "dot", "complexno": "i", "matrixparens": "[", "inversetrig": "cos-1", "logicsymbol": "lang", "sqrtsign": true}, "nhints": 0, "questiontext": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px\"><p>For the following function, what is the domain determined by the domain convention?</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ f({{CT:0}}) = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{{CT:1}}-{{CT:2}} -{{CT:0}}^2}} . \\]</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:14px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><p>Give your answer as a logical sequence of inequalities such as \"<code dir=\"ltr\">x&lt;=-11 or x&gt;13</code>\".</p><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">[[input:ans1]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans1]]</div></div></div>", "generalfeedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:12px 16px;margin-bottom:12px\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Outline:</b> The expression under the root, which is in the denominator, must be strictly positive; factor the quadratic and find where it is positive.</div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 1 — The condition</b><br>For the function to exist, the square root must exist and cannot be <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(0\\)</span>, hence<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {{CT:1}}-{{CT:2}} -{{CT:0}}^2 = -({{CT:0}} + {{CT:3}})({{CT:0}} - {{CT:4}}) &gt; 0. \\]</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 2 — The domain</b><br>The left-hand side is a downward parabola with zeros <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(-{{CT:3}}\\)</span> and <span dir=\"ltr\">\\({{CT:4}}\\)</span>, so it is positive strictly between them. This is the case when<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ -{{CT:3}} &lt; {{CT:0}} &lt; {{CT:4}} \\]</p>This is entered as <span dir=\"ltr\">\\({{CT:0}} \\gt -{{CT:3}}\\)</span> and <span dir=\"ltr\">\\({{CT:0}}\\lt {{CT:4}}\\)</span>: enter <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(-{{CT:3}} &lt; {{CT:0}} \\mbox{ and } {{CT:0}} &lt; {{CT:4}}.\\)</span></div></div>", "specificfeedback": "<p>[[feedback:Result]]</p>", "prtcorrect": "<p><span class=\"correct\">Correct answer, well done.</span></p>", "prtpartiallycorrect": "<p><span class=\"partially\">Your answer is partially correct.</span></p>", "prtincorrect": "<p><span class=\"incorrect\">Incorrect answer.</span></p>", "inputs": [{"name": "ans1", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 20, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": "", "requirelowestterms": true}], "prts": [{"name": "Result", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "ta1", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 1, "penalty": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "Result-0-T ", "feedback": ""}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "penalty": 0, "nextnode": 1, "answernote": "Result-0-F ", "feedback": ""}}, {"name": 1, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "ta2", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "penalty": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "Result-2-T", "feedback": ""}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "penalty": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "Result-2-F", "feedback": ""}}]}], "qvnames": ["n1", "n2", "ta1", "ta2", "v"], "nvariants": 20}